What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/mt6350-usb/state
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	FuQuan <i@fuquan.moe>
Description:
		Read-only cached physical USB VBUS detector state. irq is the Linux
		mapping for MT6350 CHRDET hwirq 10; events counts interrupt callbacks.
		online uses CHRSTATUS[4], valid records a successful sample, and error
		is the last regmap/extcon errno. con0 and chrstatus retain raw 16-bit
		status words for diagnostics. No PMIC access is made by this attribute.
		wake_armed means this suspend armed CHRDET in the parent's wake mask;
		it returns to zero on resume. power/wakeup controls board wake policy.
		EXTCON_USB reports VBUS presence, not USB speed, data connection or
		charger classification. Interrupts request a bounded 5-second wake
		window for USB enumeration and charger status updates. Charging current
		and battery policy remain owned by the existing supply drivers.
